 "quality_verdict": {
  "overall": "REJECTED. The repair is a real but partial improvement: measurably sharper interior textures and a visibly faster 4/16 -> 16/16 recovery, with no ringing or halos seen. It does not reach nearest-DRS texture detail, leaves thin-geometry blinking and sprite/text softness exactly unchanged, and worsens the C7 disocclusion residual numerically. OWN remains visually indistinguishable from ordinary UP.",
  "accepted_parts": [
   "visibly faster detail recovery on the third and fourth 16/16 frames after 4/16",
   "measurably higher interior texture contrast at 8/16 without visible ringing",
   "no added temporal darkness measured inside or beside the step-20 shadow on the sign"
  ],
  "rejected_parts": [
   "texture detail still far below DRS (2-texel checker 4.6-7.0 vs DRS 26.0 codes)",
   "thin wires blink exactly as before (deferred mixed-clear history; 4-row jitter lattice)",
   "sprites and world text unchanged: current-only overlays upsampled bilinearly by composite.wgsl",
   "C7 worst trailing column up about 24% (UP 0.050 -> 0.062, OWN 0.053 -> 0.065 at step 20)",
   "larger pops at the 4->16 and 16->8 switches",
   "OWN falls back to bilinear on changed owners (all owners on a first frame, moving owners), so it gains nothing over UP there"
  ]
 },
